# Roadmap

Legend: `[x]` done (implemented and tested) · `[~]` partial · `[ ]` not started

## Phase 1 — Foundation
- [x] Repository, packaging metadata, modular architecture (Qt-free core)
- [x] PySide6 application, main window, menus, classic toolbar, docks, status bar
- [x] Canvas with root topic; add / edit / delete topics; multi-line text
- [x] Drag-and-drop re-parenting and reordering
- [x] Zoom (buttons, wheel, pinch) and pan
- [x] Undo/redo through commands; macros are one step
- [x] Save/open the universal `.vmap` format (hardened, atomic)
- [x] Basic theme system (4 built-ins, import/export, per-topic overrides)
- [x] Automated tests (core, formats, CLI, layout, performance, headless GUI)
- [x] README and architecture documentation
- [ ] Manual verification on Linux, Windows and macOS hardware *(please report results)*

## Phase 2 — Structures and map objects
- [~] Structures: mind map, logic chart, left map done; org chart, tree, timeline, fishbone, matrix, brace, radial, circle and the rest still to do
- [ ] Relationships · [ ] Boundaries · [ ] Summaries · [ ] Floating topics · [ ] Callouts
- [~] Labels and markers (in the data model; no UI yet)
- [~] Styles (topic overrides done; per-branch inheritance editor still to do)
- [ ] Numbering, topic filtering, task topics, theme editor UI

## Phase 3 — Vector graphics and media
- [ ] Vector shapes, paths, Bézier curves, grouping, alignment, snapping, guides, layers
- [ ] SVG import/embed/convert · [ ] Images, attachments, equations, rich-text notes · [ ] Asset Manager

## Phase 4 — Open formats
- [ ] XMind (legacy and XMind 8 era) · [ ] FreeMind · [ ] Freeplane · [ ] OPML · [ ] Markdown · [ ] TextBundle
- [ ] Round-trip compatibility suite with measured percentages
- [ ] `vmap import/export/convert/render/batch`

## Phase 5 — Proprietary formats
Only where documented or legally possible: MindManager, MindNode, MindMeister, MindMup,
Coggle, GitMind, EdrawMind. Each is clearly reported as full or partial support.

## Phase 6 — Productivity views
- [ ] Outliner · [ ] Presentation mode · [ ] Brainstorming · [ ] Gantt / tasks · [ ] Printing · [ ] PDF/DOCX/XLSX/PPTX export

## Phase 7 — AI providers
- [ ] Provider abstraction · OpenAI-compatible · Anthropic · Google · Mistral · OpenRouter · Ollama · LM Studio · llama.cpp
- [ ] API keys in the OS keychain only

## Phase 8 — AI features
- [ ] Text→map, AI chat panel aware of the selection, previewed AI edits applied as one undo step
- [ ] Document→map, image→map (OCR/vision), web→map (respecting robots.txt and access controls)

## Phase 9 — Platform
- [ ] Plugin SDK (entry points, manifests) · [ ] MCP server · [ ] Collaboration architecture (operation log / CRDT)
- [ ] Optional asset packs (`.lpack`) with licence metadata and `asset-license-check`

## Phase 10 — Release
- [ ] Installers: AppImage, .deb, .rpm, Flatpak, Windows installer + portable ZIP, macOS .app/.dmg
- [ ] Code signing, optional updater with rollback, autosave, crash recovery, version history
- [ ] Classic / Modern UI modes, customisable shortcuts, shipped translations (incl. Persian, Arabic)
